menu "BlueAudio Puck: link monitoring"

    config PUCK_RSSI_POLL_SECONDS
        int "Seconds between link quality reads"
        default 3
        range 1 60
        help
            How often the puck asks the controller how the link is doing, so
            the signal meter can move.

            Bluetooth Classic does not report absolute signal strength. It
            reports a delta from the Golden Receive Power Range, so zero means
            "healthy", not "no signal". A good link reads zero and the meter
            sits full; the value only goes negative once the link is actually
            struggling. Treat the bars as fine / getting worse / about to drop
            out, not as dBm.

endmenu
